ows=[code], callbackURLs=[admin URL], logoutURLs=[...] }\\\\n• Custom attributes: dwelling_unit (String, mutable), invitation_role (String, immutable).  invitation_role used to auto-assign group at confirmation.\\\\n• Standard attribute mappings into tokens: sub, email, email_verified, phone_number, name.\\\\n• Pre-Token Generation Lambda injects claims: { \\\\\\\"dwelling_unit\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"cognito:groups\\\\\\\" } so front-end can authorize UI elements.\\\\n\\\\n2. User Pool Groups\\\\n• residents     – Default for self-registrations.\\\\n• board-members – Elevated; requires admin invitation.\\\\n• admins        – Highest; Cognito administrators + App/Infra admins.\\\\nEach group maps to a distinct IAM role in the Identity Pool (see §3) via Role Mapping.\\\\n\\\\n3. Identity Pool (Cognito Federated Identities)\\\\n• Name: HOA_IdentityPool, allowUnauthenticatedIdentities=true (for public-only site access)\\\\n• Authentication providers: cognito-idp.<region>.amazonaws.com/<UserPoolId>\\\\n• Role mapping: Token-based, precedence = groups>\\\\n  – residents ⇒ Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role\\\\n  – board-members ⇒ Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role\\\\n  – admins ⇒ Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role\\\\n  – unauthenticated ⇒ Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role\\\\n• IAM roles & key policy snippets:\\\\n  a) Cognito_HOAResidentsAuth_Role  – read-only S3 objects in bucket hoa-public & hoa-resident, execute API Gateway invoke-only (GET /minutes, GET /news).\\\\n  b) Cognito_HOABoardAuth_Role      – R/W S3 on hoa-board, invoke all HOA API, DynamoDB read on HOA_Documents.\\\\n  c) Cognito_HOAAdminsAuth_Role     – Full access to HOA API, S3 buckets, DocumentDB, CloudWatch logs; no IAM:*.\\\\n  d) Cognito_HOAUnauth_Role         – Read-only S3 on hoa-public, invoke GET /news.\\\\n\\\\n4. Front-end Integration Strategy\\\\n• Use AWS Amplify Auth or cognito-identity-js. Store id & access tokens ONLY in memory; refresh token in secure, httpOnly, sameSite=strict cookie issued by a CloudFront-signed backend (/auth/refresh) to mitigate XSS.\\\\n• Automatic token refresh via Cookie-stored refresh_token + /token endpoint every 50 min.\\\\n• SPA adds Authorization: Bearer <idToken> header for API Gateway (JWT authorizer referencing User Pool).\\\\n• On sign-out or idle >15 min: call GlobalSignOut & delete cookies/local data.\\\\n\\\\n5. User Registration / Invitation Workflow\\\\nSelf-Registration (residents)\\\\n  1) User fills sign-up form (email, name, dwelling_unit, pwd).\\\\n  2) Pre-Sign-Up Lambda validates email domain (e.g., endsWith \\\\\\\"@somehoa.com\\\\\\\") OR cross-checks dwelling_unit against on-file resident roster (DynamoDB HOA_Residences). Reject if mismatch.\\\\n  3) Auto-confirm email via Cognito if roster matched; else email verification code.\\\\n  4) Post-Confirmation Lambda places user in 'residents' group and sends Welcome email via SES template.\\\\n\\\\nInvitation (board-members & admins)\\\\n  1) Admin clicks \\\\\\\"Invite\\\\\\\" in HOA Admin Console → triggers AdminCreateUser API with invitation_role=\\\\\\\"board\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"admin\\\\\\\".\\\\n  2) Cognito sends invitation email (customized) with temp password.\\\\n  3) On first login, ForcePwdChange; Post-Confirmation adds user to proper group, enforces MFA setup flow before issuing tokens (Define-Auth-Challenge pipeline).\\\\n\\\\n6. Password Reset & Account Recovery\\\\n• ForgotPassword API → email code (SES). Confirmation codes valid 24 h. Attempt throttling: 5 per hour.\\\\n• AccountRecoverySetting: email first, SMS second (for board & admins). Residents email-only.\\\\n• AdminResetUserPassword for help-desk.\\\\n• Post-Authentication Lambda can trigger password policy re-validation and force update if policy changes.\\\\n\\\\n7. Session Management & Security Best Practices\\\\n• Access/Id token TTL 60 min; refresh TTL 30 d; refresh revoked at GlobalSignOut.\\\\n• AdvancedSecurity: risk-based adaptive MFA, compromised creds protection.\\\\n• Device remembering disabled (not needed